id: pm-wq9njf
title: "A mutation payload nested about 2,000 levels deep overflows the secret guard's recursive leaf walk, so block mode fails open and lets a nested credential through"
description: "Found 2026-11-17 while fixing pm-3fbj1f. scanMutationSecrets in src/sdk/mutation-guard.ts collects string leaves with a recursive walk (stringLeaves, recursion through Array.prototype.flatMap). A payload nested about 2,000 levels deep exceeds the call stack (measured on Node 26 with { token: { token: ... { note: \"<credential>\" } } }: RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded). evaluateMutationGuard catches every scanner exception and fails open by design (warning secret_guard_scan_failed_open, no findings), so in block mode a deeply nested credential is not blocked; only the advisory warning remains. JSON.parse accepts far deeper nesting, so an MCP or SDK payload can reach this depth. The failure is the traversal's own limit, not a detector failure the fail-open policy was written for. Fix direction: walk the payload with an explicit stack (keeping depth-first leaf order, so existing finding order is unchanged), apply the same to the key-named member pass added by pm-3fbj1f, and pin a depth well beyond the old limit in the guard spec. Whether a genuine detector failure should fail closed in block mode is a separate policy decision and out of scope. Duplicate check: searched secret guard fail open deep nesting stack overflow payload; pm-3fbj1f, pm-gh1699 and pm-jcz7qz are related and none owns traversal depth."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:sdk",mcp,robustness,secret-guard,security
created_at: "2026-11-17T00:11:55.697Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T02:01:32.116Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-17T02:01:27.493Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-17T02:01:27.493Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "scanMutationSecrets walks string leaves and key-named members with an explicit stack, so a payload nested far deeper than the call stack (at least 100,000 levels) is scanned without an exception; Findings keep their depth-first order and paths, so existing guard specs pass unchanged; In block mode a credential nested at that depth is blocked instead of producing secret_guard_scan_failed_open"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "stringLeaves and scanPayloadMembers walk with an explicit stack, read arrays through their own index properties (never payload-owned methods, non-enumerable elements included, indices below 2^32 - 1), and findings dedupe through a Set with depth-first order kept"
expected_result: A payload nested far deeper than the call stack is scanned without an exception and its credential is blocked in block mode
actual_result: "A 100,000-level payload is scanned in about 430 ms and block mode throws mutation_secret_guard_blocked; depth-first finding order, hostile array methods and sparse arrays are pinned in the spec"
component: secret-guard
